.TH WOTAN\-CTL 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 648a2501" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
wotan\-ctl \- Load MBC bytecode, memory images and boot state into the Wotan BPF compute engine.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wotan\-ctl
COMMAND [OPTION]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Load MBC bytecode, memory images and boot state into the Wotan BPF compute engine.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B boot
Load and boot a UPC kernel image
.TP
.B doom
Doom\-over\-IPv6 compute engine management
.TP
.B load\-mem
Load binary data into Wotan's L2 ring buffer (RAM)
.TP
.B load\-rom
Load MBC bytecode into BPF rom_map
.TP
.B mkfs
Format a UNFS ramdisk filesystem
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH NOTES
Run "wotan\-ctl COMMAND \-\-help" for a command's options. BPF maps are read from /sys/fs/bpf.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
wotan\-ctl load\-rom \-file prog.mbc         load bytecode into rom_map
wotan\-ctl boot \-\-help                     UPC boot options
wotan\-ctl doom status                     Doom\-over\-IPv6 state
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
